# Ashraf Project – Courier Business Platform: Frontend Design Phase 1

## Objective

Build the complete frontend UI for the first stage of the Courier Business Platform, strictly following the provided user flowchart.  
**No backend logic or API integration—focus is on layout, navigation, and user experience.**

---

## 1. Technology & Design System

- **Framework:** Next.js 14+ (App Router)
- **Language:** TypeScript
- **Styling:** Tailwind CSS only
- **UI Components:** shadcn/ui (https://ui.shadcn.com/)
- **State Management:** Zustand (for client-side state, if needed)
- **Transitions:** Use premium, subtle transitions as per premium-transitions-and-effects.mdc
- **Accessibility:** All UI must be accessible (ARIA, keyboard navigation, color contrast)

---

## 2. Scope & Requirements

### Pages & Components (All UI, No Backend)
- Merchant Landing Page (Login/Signup)
- Create Account (email, password, business info)
- Email Verification (mock)
- Secure Login (with optional 2FA UI)
- Merchant Dashboard (main hub)
- **[Shopify integration and related UI are excluded from this phase. Do NOT implement or mock any Shopify-related flows, forms, or components.]**
- Create New Shipment (manual form)
- Enter Package Details (form)
- Generate Real-time Quote (mock)
- Purchase Label (mock Stripe UI)
- Generate 4x6 PDF Label (mock preview)
- Download & Print Label (button)
- Find Drop-off Location (Google Maps UI placeholder)
- Drop Package at Location (confirmation UI)
- Courier Scans Barcode (mock UI)
- Tracking Updates (mock status)
- AI Route Optimization (mock UI)
- Courier Out for Delivery (mock status)
- Photo Proof of Delivery (mock upload UI)
- Upload to Supabase Storage (mock)
- Tracking Update: Delivered (mock)
- Merchant Views Proof (dashboard)
- Analytics & Reporting (mock charts)
- Admin Panel (Super Admin access, mock)
- Manage All Accounts (mock)
- Platform Analytics (mock)
- Operational Management (mock)

---

## 3. Navigation

- Use Next.js App Router for all navigation.
- All flows must match the provided user flowchart (excluding Shopify).
- All navigation and state changes handled client-side (no server calls).

---

## 4. Data & Logic

- All data is static, mocked, or placeholder.
- No API calls, no backend logic, no authentication.
- Use mock data for lists, forms, and status updates.

---

## 5. Code Quality & Structure

- Use TypeScript everywhere.
- Functional components only.
- Early returns, no dead code, no TODOs.
- Descriptive naming and clear structure.
- All forms, buttons, and flows must be visually complete and accessible.

---

## 6. Deliverables

- All pages and components as per the flowchart (excluding Shopify).
- Fully navigable UI demo (no backend).
- README update with instructions for running the frontend demo.

---

## 7. Enforcement

- Code reviews must verify adherence to this rule file and referenced standards.
- Any deviation must be documented and approved by the project lead.

---

**Note:**  
**Shopify integration and related UI will be covered in a subsequent development phase. Do NOT include any Shopify-related features in this stage.**

---

**Goal:**  
Deliver a pixel-perfect, accessible, and modern UI foundation for the Courier Business Platform, ready for future backend/API integration.

